-- name    : Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree
-- status  : Definition
-- author  : @Claude
-- created : 2026-09-05T04:28:28.084567+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/32e19ef2-2b4c-5dc0-b59d-3efb1060a898
-- title:
--   Degree of K(X) over K(Xn) and over K(X)ℓ
-- statement:
--   This module computes the degree of a rational function field over the subfield generated by a power of the variable, and identifies the image of Frobenius when the constants are perfect.
--
--   For a field $K$ and $n : \mathbb{N}$, [`RatFunc.finrank_adjoin_X_pow`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L158) states that $K(X)$ has $K$-dimension $n$ over the intermediate field $K(X^n)$, obtained from the numerator and denominator of $X^n$ (computed by [`RatFunc.num_X_pow`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L140), [`RatFunc.denom_X_pow`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L144), [`RatFunc.intDegree_X_pow`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L148)). For $n \neq 0$, [`RatFunc.X_pow_ne_C`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L152) says $X^n$ is not a constant, hence $X$ is integral over $K(X^n)$ ([`RatFunc.isIntegral_adjoin_X_pow`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L165)), and [`RatFunc.powerBasisAdjoinXPow`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L171) is the resulting power basis of $K(X)$ over $K(X^n)$; its generator is $X$, its dimension is $n$, and its $i$-th basis vector is $X^i$.
--
--   In characteristic $\ell$ a prime, [`RatFunc.intDegree_pow`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L200) and [`RatFunc.pow_ne_X`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L209) (for $n \ge 2$) give that $X$ is not an $\ell$-th power, so the field range of `frobenius (RatFunc K) ℓ` is a proper subfield. If moreover $K$ is perfect (a `PerfectRing K ℓ` instance), [`RatFunc.mem_fieldRange_frobenius_iff`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L247) and [`RatFunc.fieldRange_frobenius_eq_toSubfield_adjoin`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L281) identify $K(X)^\ell$ with $K(X^\ell)$, whence [`RatFunc.finrank_fieldRange_frobenius`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L288): $[K(X) : K(X)^\ell] = \ell$.
--
--   Transport results accompany this: [`Subfield.finrank_map_ringEquiv`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L34) and [`map_fieldRange_frobenius`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L46) show that a ring isomorphism carries the Frobenius subfield to the Frobenius subfield and preserves the degree ([`finrank_fieldRange_frobenius_eq_of_ringEquiv`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L58)), while [`finrank_fieldRange_frobenius_eq_of_finiteDimensional`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L70) proves $[F:F^\ell] = [K:K^\ell]$ for $F/K$ finite of characteristic $\ell$, by a multiplicativity argument for `Subfield.relfinrank` applied to the chain $K^\ell \subseteq K \cap F^\ell$ inside $F$; [`finrank_fieldRange_frobenius_eq_of_isSeparable`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L125) is the same statement with a separability instance added. Finally, for an algebra endomorphism $\varphi$ of $F$ with $\varphi(x) = x^\ell$ for all $x$, [`AlgHom.finrank_fieldRange_of_forall_pow`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L302) and its two corollaries give $[F : \varphi(F)] = \ell$ when $F$ is finite over a field isomorphic to a rational function field over a perfect field of characteristic $\ell$. Small helper bridges relate `IntermediateField` and `Subfield` degrees, the field range of `algebraMap`, and membership of `aeval` values in a simple adjunction; the closing statements instantiate the computation at $K = \mathbb{F}_2$, $\ell = 2$.
--
--   **Relation to Mathlib.** All declarations live in Mathlib namespaces and build on Mathlib's theory of `RatFunc` (`finrank_eq_max_natDegree`, `adjoin_X`, `IntermediateField.adjoinXEquiv`), `PerfectRing`, and `Subfield.relfinrank`; nothing new is defined beyond the power basis [`RatFunc.powerBasisAdjoinXPow`](../def/Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.html#L171) and the added lemmas.
--
--   **Where it is used.** The imperfection degree computation is used where an endomorphism acting as $x \mapsto x^\ell$ on a field finite over a rational function field in characteristic $\ell$ must be shown to have image of index exactly $\ell$, supplying a rank input to a finiteness verification elsewhere in the development.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Definitions/Def_Mathlib_FieldTheory_RatFuncImperfectionDegree.lean

